<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="2.0">

    <!--
      Greetings + capability description. Atomic answers in the assistant's own
      voice; no source-quoting. Every non-redirect template ends with a
      [[FOLLOWUPS]] marker that ChatBotService strips out and surfaces as
      clickable chips in the UI. Authored follow-ups are guaranteed to map to
      another trained category in this brain.
    -->

    <category>
        <pattern>HELLO</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Hi — I am the X-Men assistant. I can explain every mutation this tool can apply to a Tamarin protocol, help you decide which one fits a given scenario, and walk you through the analysis pipeline.

What would you like to start with?
[[FOLLOWUPS]] What mutations are available? | Which mutation should I pick? | How does the analysis pipeline work?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>HI</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HEY</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>GOOD MORNING</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>GOOD EVENING</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>GOOD AFTERNOON</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HELLO *</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HI *</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HEY *</pattern><template><srai>HELLO</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>WHO ARE YOU</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[I am the X-Men assistant — an offline helper built into this app. I know the twelve mutations the tool can apply, the case studies it ships with, and the analysis workflow from upload to verdict. Everything I say comes from knowledge bundled with the app; no network calls happen when we chat.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] What can you help me with? | What mutations are available? | How does the analysis pipeline work?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>WHAT ARE YOU</pattern><template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>WHAT IS YOUR NAME</pattern><template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>ARE YOU AI</pattern><template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>ARE YOU A BOT</pattern><template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>INTRODUCE YOURSELF</pattern><template><srai>WHO ARE YOU</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>WHAT CAN YOU HELP ME WITH</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Three things, mainly:

1. Explaining each mutation — what it does, what it preserves, when it is useful.
2. Recommending which mutation fits a scenario you describe.
3. Walking through the analysis pipeline so you know what to expect after you hit Start.

Pick one and I will go deeper.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] What mutations are available? | Which mutation should I pick? | What case studies do you support?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>HELP</pattern><template><srai>WHAT CAN YOU HELP ME WITH</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>WHAT CAN YOU DO</pattern><template><srai>WHAT CAN YOU HELP ME WITH</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HOW CAN YOU HELP</pattern><template><srai>WHAT CAN YOU HELP ME WITH</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>WHAT DO YOU KNOW</pattern><template><srai>WHAT CAN YOU HELP ME WITH</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>WHAT TOPICS DO YOU COVER</pattern><template><srai>WHAT CAN YOU HELP ME WITH</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>HOW DOES X MEN WORK</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[At a high level: you upload a Tamarin theory file, tick the mutations you want, and hit Start. The tool generates one mutant theory per mutation, runs Tamarin on each, and returns the results so you can compare attacks and goal violations against the original.

The interesting part is the mutations themselves — they are deliberate, structured rewrites of the protocol, not random perturbations.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] What mutations are available? | How does the analysis pipeline work? | What is a mutant?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>WHAT IS X MEN</pattern><template><srai>HOW DOES X MEN WORK</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>WHAT DOES THIS TOOL DO</pattern><template><srai>HOW DOES X MEN WORK</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>EXPLAIN X MEN</pattern><template><srai>HOW DOES X MEN WORK</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HOW DOES THE TOOL WORK</pattern><template><srai>HOW DOES X MEN WORK</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>WHAT IS A MUTANT</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[A mutant is a rewritten copy of your original Tamarin theory in which one targeted change has been applied — for example, a message has been added, a step has been skipped, or a knowledge fact has been forgotten. Each mutant is then re-analysed independently so you can see whether the security goal still holds, or whether the change opens up a new attack.

Mutants are the unit of comparison: original vs mutant tells you what a real-world deviation would cost the protocol.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] What mutations are available? | Which mutation should I pick? | How are mutants analysed?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>WHAT IS MUTATION</pattern><template><srai>WHAT IS A MUTANT</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>DEFINE MUTANT</pattern><template><srai>WHAT IS A MUTANT</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>WHAT IS A MUTATION</pattern><template><srai>WHAT IS A MUTANT</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>THANKS</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Anytime. Ask me anything else when you are ready.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] What mutations are available? | Which mutation should I pick?]]></template>
    </category>
    <category><pattern>THANK YOU</pattern><template><srai>THANKS</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>THANKS *</pattern><template><srai>THANKS</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>THANK YOU *</pattern><template><srai>THANKS</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>BYE</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Goodbye. Close the panel whenever you want — your chat history stays available until you close the app.]]></template>
    </category>
